{"name":"Red Crayon","hex":"#ee204d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"},{"term":"crayon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A stick of colored chalk or wax used for drawing.","A colored pencil, a colouring pencil"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To draw with a crayon."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crayon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Crayon","blocks":[{"text":"A crayon is a stick of pigmented wax used for writing or drawing. Wax crayons differ from pastels, in which the pigment is mixed with a dry binder such as gum arabic, and from oil pastels, where the binder is a mixture of wax and oil."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Crayones_cera.jpg/330px-Crayones_cera.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crayon","wikidata":"Q69158"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/VariousCrayonBoxes.jpg/500px-VariousCrayonBoxes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/VariousCrayonBoxes.jpg/500px-VariousCrayonBoxes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A wide variety of crayon boxes have been produced over the years.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVariousCrayonBoxes.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Dixon_Crayon_Ad.jpg/500px-Dixon_Crayon_Ad.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Dixon_Crayon_Ad.jpg/500px-Dixon_Crayon_Ad.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Early Dixon crayon ad from August 1901","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADixon_Crayon_Ad.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Crayola_Ad_1905.jpg/500px-Crayola_Ad_1905.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Crayola_Ad_1905.jpg/500px-Crayola_Ad_1905.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"March 1905 ad from Crayola","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACrayola_Ad_1905.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Crayons_%26_Drawing.jpg/500px-Crayons_%26_Drawing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Crayons_%26_Drawing.jpg/1280px-Cr